 _Part of the [ngit-grasp reference documentation](./)_
+
+### NGIT_PRIVATE_REPOSITORY_READERS_FILE
+
+Optional path, unset by default. With private mode enabled, load a JSON object
+mapping `npub/repository` to an explicit nonempty array of reader npubs. The
+coordinate owner must be included. This only narrows service membership; it
+never grants maintainership or canonical write permission. A missing coordinate
+is denied, including unknown repositories. Invalid/unreadable files fail startup.
+Git credentials are checked against both service and repository membership.
+Relay events are filtered before delivery, including broad subscriptions. All
+repository a/A tags must name readable coordinates; e-only replies are denied.
+Scoped COUNT/negentropy are disabled to prevent cross-repository existence leaks.
+Membership changes currently require a reviewed service recreation; retain the
+manifest with the service recovery backup. No content or keys belong in it.
